.flashtools/

# Raw hardware data, measurements, backups and credentials: keep local, never commit.
# Test fixtures must be synthetic (tools/check_privacy.py enforces this; tools/test_local.ps1 runs it).
*.log
!test/fixtures/**/synthetic-*.log
*.jsonl
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.cu8
*.cs16
*.iq
*.sigmf-*
logs/
captures/
measurements/
backups/
_backups/
*.bundle
*.nvs
*.mac
.env
.env.*
*credentials*

# Local pairing captures (real device IDs): never commit
captures/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ESP-IDF / Matter build (idf/, docs/MATTER.md): fetched libraries (tools/fetch_idf_deps.sh), build output, generated
# configuration. Only the wrappers in idf/components-cmake/ and the own component idf/components/orcon_matter/ are tracked.
idf/build/
idf/components/arduino/
idf/components/ArduinoJson/
idf/components/RadioLib/
idf/components/U8g2/
idf/managed_components/
test/qemu/probe/managed_components/
idf/sdkconfig
idf/sdkconfig.old
*.elf
*.map
*.map.gz
# A device's own Matter identity never belongs in the repository (tools/matter_identity.sh keeps it in ~/.orcon-matter):
# its header (DAC private key, setup code), its serial number, its pairing codes and its keys.
orcon_matter_creds.h
!idf/components/orcon_matter/placeholder/orcon_matter_creds.h
identity.defaults
KOPPELCODE.txt
*.pem
*.der
